        "text" : "**Bad debt** is the opposite: borrowing for things you don't need, things that lose value the moment you buy them and put nothing back in your pocket. When you do this, you're borrowing from your future self. You get the item now, but future-you repays it plus interest. The classic example is a credit card balance on wants you couldn't afford: a fancy outfit, a nice dinner, a gadget. It feels good now, but you may be paying it down for a very long time.",
